  "note": "The red convent and corner-pinnacled clock tower stand beside the ochre palace and its lead-colored dome. An open stone gate leads toward twin gilded cupolas above the tiled portal. The vaulted passage links the entrance side with a paved terrace and an open domed lookout. A 483.7 m sea-level datum anchors the palace to standard viewer terrain. The retaining walls extend below sampled grade and the approach crosses the gate along the mapped service route. Two mapped convent courts remain open. The replacement covers the palace and its parts while preserving nearby footprints and paths. Preview places the authored base at the recorded absolute sea-level elevation; local tide and terrain resolution remain host-dependent."
